            <ArticleTitle>Postextrasystolic changes in ventricular depolarization (electrocardiographic observations).</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>199-203</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Postextrasystolic changes in ventricular depolarization were found in patients with coronary artery disease in two situations: a) after a compensatory postextrasystolic pause and, b) after an interpolated ventricular beat. The explanation and the underlying conditions of this phenomenon are discussed. In our opinion the postextrasystolic change may be a silent myocardial ischemia.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
